---
layout: layouts/page.njk
---
{% include "partials/hero.njk" %}

{#
  Region-info shell (architecture.md §3): one shared region-card.njk partial feeds two
  render modes, switched by a width-only CSS breakpoint (768px, see --bp-region-info-wide in
  tokens.css) — never both at once, never recomputed on resize.
    - Wide (region-infographic): all 6 regions permanently visible around the map, in two
      fixed-position columns connected to the map by static, hand-positioned SVG leader lines.
      Cross-hover (card <-> map region <-> leader line) is pure CSS (:has()), no JS — each
      card/line carries a matching data-slug/data-region-slug for the selectors to key off.
      The leader-line coordinates below are authored once against a 240px column width and the
      map's own centroids; keep --infographic cards a fixed height so the lines stay aligned.
    - Narrow (region-carousel): the map alone, full width, followed by a horizontal scroll-snap
      carousel of all 6 real region-card links + dot indicators (DESIGN.md § "Region card").
      korea-map.js's tap handler scrolls the carousel to the tapped region's card instead of
      navigating straight there; every card is still a real <a href> if JS is off.
  Left/right column assignment follows each region's actual west/east position on the map
  (Gyeonggi/Chungcheong/Jeolla/Jeju sit west of the map's own centre line, Gangwon/Gyeongsang
  east), ordered N-to-S within each column.
#}
<section id="map" class="home-regions" aria-labelledby="home-regions-heading">
  <div class="home-regions__head">
    <div class="home-regions__intro">
      <h2 id="home-regions-heading">The six regions</h2>
      <p>
        Hover a region or its card to highlight it on the map — on a phone, tap the map to jump
        to a card. Open either to see the region.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ul class="map-legend" aria-label="Map colour key">
      <li class="map-legend__item"><span class="map-legend__swatch map-legend__swatch--active" aria-hidden="true"></span>Eligible</li>
      <li class="map-legend__item"><span class="map-legend__swatch map-legend__swatch--partial" aria-hidden="true"></span>Partly eligible</li>
      <li class="map-legend__item"><span class="map-legend__swatch map-legend__swatch--ineligible" aria-hidden="true"></span>Not eligible</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  {#
    Always-visible note plate (DESIGN.md § Recurring parts "Note plate") explaining the
    "Partly eligible" state — some regions are partial only in their decline-designated
    counties. The data-map-legend-detail line stays hidden until korea-map.js's applyResult()
    fills it with the specific county list after a calculator run marks a region partial.
  #}
  <div class="map-note">
    <span class="map-note__chip" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="map-note__body">
      <p class="map-note__text">
        <span class="map-note__lead">Partly eligible</span> means only a region's
        population-decline-designated counties are open to you — the rest of the province still
        needs the higher capital-area income.
        <a href="/regions/gyeonggi-do/population-decline-counties/">See Gyeonggi-do's counties →</a>
      </p>
      <p class="map-note__detail" data-map-legend-detail hidden></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="region-infographic" aria-label="Region overview">
    <div class="region-infographic__col region-infographic__col--left">
      {% for slug in ["gyeonggi-do", "chungcheong-do", "jeolla-do", "jeju-do"] %}
      {% set region = regions | findBySlug(slug) %}
      {% set cost = costOfLiving | findBySlug(slug) %}
      {% set modifier = "infographic" %}
      {% include "partials/region-card.njk" %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {% include "partials/korea-map.njk" %}

    <div class="region-infographic__col region-infographic__col--right">
      {% for slug in ["gangwon-do", "gyeongsang-do"] %}
      {% set region = regions | findBySlug(slug) %}
      {% set cost = costOfLiving | findBySlug(slug) %}
      {% set modifier = "infographic" %}
      {% include "partials/region-card.njk" %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {#
      Card columns are 270px wide (region-card.css). x1 anchors sit on the column inner edges
      (270 left, 730 right); x2 is a point inside the map. Each y1 is its card's vertical centre
      in this viewBox, pulled ~8% toward the map's own centre line (475) so the six lines read as
      a tidy fan rather than converging steeply; x2/y2 point at the region's map centroid.
      Re-derive y1 if .region-card--infographic's height changes; shift x2 with the column width.
    #}
    <svg class="region-infographic__lines" viewBox="0 0 1000 950" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <line data-slug="gyeonggi-do" x1="270" y1="142.7" x2="418.8" y2="193.5" />
      <line data-slug="chungcheong-do" x1="270" y1="364.2" x2="437.9" y2="352.6" />
      <line data-slug="jeolla-do" x1="270" y1="585.8" x2="404.5" y2="587.3" />
      <line data-slug="jeju-do" x1="270" y1="807.3" x2="345.9" y2="911.3" />
      <line data-slug="gangwon-do" x1="730" y1="364.2" x2="549.6" y2="160.2" />
      <line data-slug="gyeongsang-do" x1="730" y1="585.8" x2="589.9" y2="462.3" />
    </svg>
  </div>

  {#
    Narrow-viewport carousel: all 6 region cards as a horizontal scroll-snap row + dot
    indicators (CLAUDE.md feedback log). Hidden at >=768px where the infographic takes over.
    The dots are position indicators only for now (no scroll-sync JS yet).
  #}
  <div class="region-carousel" aria-label="All six regions">
    <ul class="region-carousel__track">
      {% for slug in ["gyeonggi-do", "gangwon-do", "chungcheong-do", "gyeongsang-do", "jeolla-do", "jeju-do"] %}
      {% set region = regions | findBySlug(slug) %}
      {% set cost = costOfLiving | findBySlug(slug) %}
      {% set modifier = "carousel" %}
      <li class="region-carousel__item">{% include "partials/region-card.njk" %}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <ol class="region-carousel__dots" aria-hidden="true">
      {% for slug in ["gyeonggi-do", "gangwon-do", "chungcheong-do", "gyeongsang-do", "jeolla-do", "jeju-do"] %}
      <li></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>

  <p class="home-regions__source">
    Rents are hand-checked from current listings in each region, September 2026 — furnished
    short-term places only. Utilities, food and transport are not included.
  </p>
</section>
